 about 57% in the three months before the base. It then formed a base for about 4 weeks, peaking at $26.42 and pulling back 13% at its deepest. Daily price ranges tightened on the right side of the base.","outcome":"On Jan 2, 2004 it closed at $26.66, its first close above the base high of $26.41. Volume that day was 2.5M shares, 1.73x the prior 10-day average of 1.4M. It held, never closing below the level three days running, reached a best close of $28.99, and the chart ends at $24.81.","lesson":"This is an example of a textbook breakout: a base, then a close above it on heavy volume, and it held. This is the pattern the rules are built around."}}